# Package
# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored. This is a published package (@ncog/necjs) and its
# CI runs `npm ci`, which cannot run at all without a committed lockfile:
#   $ git clone <repo> /tmp/x && cd /tmp/x && npm ci
#   npm error code EUSAGE -- The `npm ci` command can only install with an existing package-lock.json
# Ignoring it also meant nobody could reproduce a release install; the lockfile existed only on the
# machine that happened to have run `npm install`.

# Test output: tests/sigv2.test.ts writes the signed golden vector here on every run.
tests/testdata/
